to become a  pro hero  tanya was devastated after tensei was  critically wounded by the hero killer  stain  tensei survived but he was left  paralyzed by his injuries  and he was forced to retire from being a  hero tenya then inherited his older  brother's hero name  ingenium next up we have the student in  seat number five  ochako uraraka she was born in mia  prefecture in the kansai region of japan  and her parents own a construction  business unfortunately  ochoko's parents construction business  has been suffering  and so the family has been facing some  financial hardship  but despite these financial issues  ochoko's parents were always loving and  caring towards her  and so ochako decided that she wanted to  help her parents in fact  ochako offered to use her gravity quirk  to help with the family business  since her ability to make large objects  weightless  would be an immense advantage in any  construction project  however ochako's parents wanted their  daughter to follow her  own dreams so instead of asking her to  dedicate herself to helping the  struggling family business  they encouraged her to pursue her own  dream of becoming a hero  ochako agreed because she really wanted  to help people but she also hopes to  earn enough money as a pro hero to ease  the financial burden  of her parents in seat number six is  mashirao ojiro  also known as the guy whose quirk is  just having a big tail  i mean his quirk is literally just named  tail so yes  he has a tail that's it we don't have a  lot of information about ojiro's life  before he entered ua  we just know that he was born in tokyo  and that he has a background in martial  arts  that actually makes perfect sense since  ojiro's quirk doesn't have any cool  special powers  or abilities it's just an extra  appendage but  using martial arts allows ojiro to make  the best of his quirk by turning it  into a valuable tool in combat then we  have our boy  electric saitama also known as denki  kaminari who sits in seat number seven  coincidentally kaminari was born in  saitama prefecture  and we know that he craves positive  attention from other people especially  from girls  kaminari prioritizes socializing to his  academic studies  and he is very concerned with his public  image but even though kaminari would  love to be the coolest guy in class  he often does things that end up making  him look silly rather than cool  in seat number eight is the manliest of  hero students  ijiro kirishima like mina hirishima  is from chiba prefecture and as i  mentioned earlier  the two of them went to the same middle  school kirishima's hardening quirk  first manifested when he was only three  years old one night he woke up to pee  in the middle of the night and when he  rubbed his eyes his quirk suddenly  manifested on his hand  and the resulting injury left a scar on  his right  eye this traumatic first experience made  kirishima hate his quirk  at least initially as a kid kirishima  idolized the chivalrous hero  crimson riot who also possesses a  hardening type quirk  just like kirishima crimson riot  stresses the importance of having a  manly spirit  and being willing to train hard  regardless of how strong your quirk  is and so kirishima embraced this  philosophy  and used it as motivation to make  himself stronger hirishima knew mina in  middle school  and this was a period of his life in  which he lacked courage and confidence  mina's bravery and strong personality  inspired kirishima  and eventually he decided to change his  entire image including dying his hair  red to look more like crimson riot  kirishima eventually adopted the hero  name  red riot as a tribute to his favorite  hero  next up is koji koda also known as the  petting hero anima who sits in seat  number  nine koda hails from iwate prefecture  and he is a shy and quiet guy who  appears to be more comfortable around  nature and animals than around  humans in fact koda is so quiet that  even though class 1a was first  introduced in chapter 5  of the manga koda doesn't have his first  line of dialogue until  chapter 66. koda's quirk gives him the  ability to communicate with  and command animals but ironically  he has an extreme fear of bugs this  proves to be a challenge for koda at  first  because manipulating bugs could be a  very useful ability  if only he can overcome his phobia of  bugs  we don't know much more about his  backstory other than the fact that he  has a loving  mother who is very proud and supportive  of her son  then we have rikidosato also known as  sugarman who sits in seat number 10.  sato was born in the tottori prefecture  of japan  and we know that he is a very skilled  baker baking is of course related to his  quirk  sugar rush but it also appears to be  somewhat of a passion for sato  however when his classmates pointed out  just how good his baking was  satos seemed surprised since he didn't  think that his baking skills were  anything special this might suggest that  he comes from a baking family  perhaps baking is his family's business  and so sato grew up comparing himself to  other skilled bakers in his family  and that is why he doesn't think that  his own skills are anything special  that is just speculation though because  we really don't know much about sato's  backstory  at this point in time in seat number 11  we have  mezo shoji who was born in fukuoka  prefecture  we know that shoji is not materialistic  and that he is fine with having  only a few possessions this suggests  that he comes from a family of modest  means  and that he likely had a very humble  childhood we also know that growing up  shoji faced prejudice and discrimination  as a result of his unique appearance  shoji's mutant type quirk makes his  appearance permanently different  from that of ordinary people and so  according to shoji  people were often frightened by his  physical appearance  this is why shoji wears a mask over his  face  at all times at one point in his past  the sight of his face had made a little  girl cry  and so shoji decided to always cover his  face so that it never causes sadness to  anyone else  as a result we still have no idea what  shoji actually looks like beneath his  mask  this in itself is pretty sad shoji feels  like he has to cover his face for the  sake of others  but the fact that he is willing to do  this in the first place also speaks to  the kind of person that he is  despite his intimidating appearance  shoji  is actually a very kind and  compassionate person  next up is the rock star of class 1a kyo  kajiro who sits in seat number 12.  hailing from shizuoka prefecture kyoka  comes from a family of musicians  and she grew up with music as an  important part of her life  she can sing and play multiple  instruments and her parents were hoping  that kyouka would become a musician like  them but even though kyouka loves  music her dream was to become a hero so  that she could dedicate her life to  helping  other people ultimately kyouka's parents  supported her decision to choose her own  path and become a hero  rather than a musician then we have flex  tape spider-man himself  han tasero who sits in seat number 13.  cerro was born in tokyo and he is a very  friendly and social guy  although he is not as forward about it  as minata and kaminari  sero definitely has a strong interest in  the ladies  and in general he is a fun guy to be  around  although we don't know much about his  background we do know that horikoshi  came up with the idea for his  quirk while shopping in a convenience  store and horikoshi has also stated that  serosquirk  is one of his personal favorites in seat  number 14  we have the one and only chicken of  darkness fumikage  tokoyami comes from shizuoka prefecture  and he is a very quiet reserved and  independent guy  tokoyami has an affinity for darkness  and he is often jokingly referred to as  an  emo by the mha fanbase because of his  fashion sense and his  taste in room decor he is also very  interested in things like fantasy and  the occult  so he's kind of a cool dark emo nerd  we still haven't gotten a proper deep  dive into tokoyami's backstory but we  can assume that his quiet and  introspective personality is a result of  his appearance  and his quirk tokuyami probably faced  prejudice and discrimination for his  bird-like appearance  and since his quirk dark shadow is the  type of quirk that can go berserk  it's likely that some of the other kids  were afraid of tokoyami during his  childhood  as a result tokoyami probably retreated  into himself  and developed his own unique interests  and identity without relying on the  approval of others  next up we have shoto todoroki who sits  in seat number 15  and whose backstory has actually been  explored at great length  shoto's father is of course the former  number two and current number one pro  hero  endeavor shoto also has three  older siblings two brothers and one  sister  shoto's father spent most of his life  desperately trying to surpass all might  and when he eventually realized that  this would be impossible endeavour  decided to find a wife with the ideal  quirk  and then raise children who would one  day surpass all might  so endeavour married rey in what is  known as a quirk  marriage endeavour believed that rey's  ice-based quirk would be an ideal  pairing with his flame-based quirk  and rey's family thought that a union  with the wealthy and prominent todoroki  family  would be a solution to their financial  troubles rey  agreed to the marriage out of a sense of  duty to her family  but this was very much a marriage of  convenience rather than love  after the first three todoroki children  didn't quite possess the ideal quirks  that endeavour was looking for he was  finally satisfied with the quirk of his  fourth child shoto who had the unique  ability to use both fire  and ice endeavor was convinced that  shoto would one day surpass  all might so endeavour separated shoto  from the rest of his siblings  and instead of letting him play with his  brothers and sister endeavour pushed  shoto to train  constantly in order to get stronger in  the process of training shoto  endeavour also neglected his other  children and his relationship with his  wife ray became  strained shoto himself began to resent  his father because of his treatment of  rey  and also because he wouldn't let shoto  have a normal childhood things only got  worse  after shoto's oldest brother toya was  presumed to have been killed  in a horrible fire the tragedy led  endeavour to focus even more obsessively  on training shoto  and it also led rey to lose her mental  stability after rey suffered a mental  breakdown and poured boiling water on  shoto's face  she ended up in a mental institution  shoto blamed endeavour for everything  that happened to his mother  and to his entire family and he spent  much of his life completely rejecting  his father  for a long time he even refused to use  the flame side of his quirk  because it came from his father but  eventually shoto came to accept  both sides of his quirk and since then  he has made some slow but significant  progress  in reconciling with endeavor then we  have the invisible girl  toru hagakure who sits in seat number  16.  very little is known about toru other  than the fact that she was born in tokyo  and that both of her parents apparently  have the same invisibility type quirk as  she does  toru has a bubbly personality and she  loves to hang out with the class  1a girls gossip about boys go shopping  and all of that fun teenage girl stuff  since toru is permanently invisible  we don't know what she actually looks  like and because her quirk is so perfect  for  covert activities many mha fans believe  that toru might be the ua traitor who is  leaking vital information about the ua  to the league  of villains however there is no real  evidence for this  and the story hasn't really mentioned  the traitor in a long time  so at this point many of us are  wondering whether the traitor thing  is even a thing anymore in seat number  17  we have the legendary lord explosion  murder himself  katsuki bakugo bakugo comes from the  same neighborhood  in shizuoka prefecture as deku does and  the two of them grew up together  deku always looked up to bakugo since  bakugou had a lot of confidence and a  cool explosion quirk that always  impressed everyone  eventually all of that praise went to  bakugo's head  and he became arrogant and sometimes  downright mean  he actually gave izuku midoriya the  nickname deku  but he meant it to be an insult although  deku eventually just  embraced the nickname and even made it  his official hero name  bakugo was also a big fan of almight  just like deku  and he aspired to one day become the  kind of ultimate winner  that almight was the young bakugo firmly  believed that a great hero will always  win  no matter what and all might was the  embodiment  of that principle by the time that he  got to middle school  bakugo became an outright bully and he  would often lose his temper and berate  and abuse others  including deku since deku was born  without a quirk  bakugo often mocked deku's ambition to  get into ua and become a hero  so yeah bakugo went through a phase in  which he was an arrogant bully who was  constantly followed around by  butt-kissing  lackeys thankfully he did eventually  emerge out of that phase and develop as  a character  although he continues to have a wild  temper and a short fuse  oh and he has a hot mom yes i said it  no regrets next up in seat number 18  is the protagonist of our story the one  and only izuku midoriya  also known as deku hailing from shizuoka  prefecture just like bakugou  deku began to idolize all might at a  very young  age and it was his greatest dream in  life to become a hero  like all might unfortunately deku was  born without a quirk  in a world where the vast majority of  people possess quirks 